=== Python Orthogonality Probe ===

  int + int = 3   OK
  float + float = 3.0   OK
  str + str = 'ab'   OK
  list + list = [1, 2]   OK

  int * int = 12   OK
  float * float = 12.0   OK
  str * int = 'hahaha'   OK
  list * int = [1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2]   OK
  list * list -> TypeError: can't multiply sequence by non-int of type 'list'  FAIL

=== '==' Comparison Orthogonality ===
  1 == 1  ->  True
  1 == 1.0  ->  True
  1 == '1'  ->  False
  [] == []  ->  True
  {} == {}  ->  True
  None == False  ->  False
  0 == False  ->  True

=== Container + Operator Asymmetry ===
  set | set = {1, 2, 3}   (union)  OK
  set + set -> TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'set' and 'set'  FAIL
  dict | dict = {'a': 1, 'b': 2}  OK
  dict + dict -> TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'dict' and 'dict'  FAIL
